WEBVTT

00:00:00.421 --> 00:00:01.145
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:01.594 --> 00:00:03.110
Verb first

00:00:04.016 --> 00:00:04.750
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 1

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:11.287
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> £150 for a T-shirt? That’s a complete rip<b>-off</b>!

00:00:13.215 --> 00:00:13.938
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 2

00:00:14.961 --> 00:00:19.876
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> After insisting he could negotiate a new deal, he was forced into a climb<b>down</b>.

00:00:21.726 --> 00:00:22.526
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 3

00:00:23.591 --> 00:00:29.214
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> After ten years out of the sport, he’s made an amazing come<b>back</b> and reached the final.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:31.899
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 4

00:00:32.823 --> 00:00:38.498
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> After years of research into a cure for the disease, they have finally had a break<b>through</b>.

00:00:40.194 --> 00:00:41.046
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 5

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.191
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Family break-<b>ups</b> increase the risk of childhood depression.

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:47.915
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 6

00:00:48.759 --> 00:00:52.807
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I find musicals a bit of a turn-<b>off</b>. They’re just not my cup of tea.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.392
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 7

00:00:56.487 --> 00:01:01.403
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I’m afraid there’s been a bit of a mix-<b>up</b>. I think I’ve got your case and you’ve got mine.

00:01:03.716 --> 00:01:04.441
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 8

00:01:05.355 --> 00:01:09.396
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I’ve only been in the job a couple of weeks, so I still don’t really know the set<b>-up</b>.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.060
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 9

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.425
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> It was a bit of a let<b>-down</b> when my friends cancelled at the last minute.

00:01:18.143 --> 00:01:18.908
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 10

00:01:19.851 --> 00:01:23.804
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Nobody was hurt in the accident, but my car’s a complete write<b>-of</b>f.

00:01:25.596 --> 00:01:26.454
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 11

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.755
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The police called for back<b>up</b> when they were unable to cope with the violent crowd.

00:01:33.539 --> 00:01:34.434
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 12

00:01:35.487 --> 00:01:40.063
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> She pretended she liked her present, but her expression was a real give<b>away</b>.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:42.824
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 13

00:01:43.826 --> 00:01:47.898
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Sorry, we’re going to be about 20 minutes late. There’s a hold<b>-up</b> on the motorway.

00:01:49.739 --> 00:01:50.750
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 14

00:01:51.826 --> 00:01:55.740
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> There was a really good turn<b>out</b> for the march – over 50,000 people.

00:01:57.614 --> 00:01:58.637
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 15

00:01:59.548 --> 00:02:02.661
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The shop’s had a make<b>over</b> and it’s now much more modern.

00:02:04.686 --> 00:02:05.784
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 16

00:02:06.666 --> 00:02:10.302
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> The team suffered a major set<b>back</b> when their captain was injured.

00:02:12.069 --> 00:02:13.159
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 17

00:02:14.263 --> 00:02:18.359
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> There has been a break<b>down</b> in communication between the government and the unions.

00:02:20.352 --> 00:02:21.292
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 18

00:02:22.312 --> 00:02:26.759
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> We chose the restaurant because it had a really good write<b>-up</b> on Tripadvisor.

00:02:28.563 --> 00:02:29.704
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 19

00:02:30.698 --> 00:02:35.358
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> We’re just waiting to be given the go<b>-ahead</b> before we start working on the new project.

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:38.006
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 20

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:42.941
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> We’re on stand<b>by</b> for the evening flight – let’s hope there are some free seats.

00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:45.884
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> 21

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:52.601
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> When my boss saw the sales figures, she had a complete melt<b>down</b> and started shouting at us.